{"episodes":{"210600":"A lead-wave disturbance triggered scattered thunderstorms across east-central Oklahoma around midday on the 1st. Sufficient wind shear and instability allowed for storm organization and a few reports of large hail from a supercell thunderstorm here.","210975":"Strong to severe thunderstorms developed across portions of northeastern Oklahoma during the early to mid afternoon of March 1st, north of a warm front as an upper level disturbance approached the region. The strongest thunderstorms produced large hail up to quarter size.","212215":"A large area of showers and thunderstorms developed during the late morning hours of March 1st across central and eastern Kansas. A singular thunderstorm became severe across McPherson and Marion counties and produced multiple reports of large hail.","212439":"Severe thunderstorms developed along an outflow boundary propagating southward across eastern Florida Bay, resulting in large hail and damaging winds.  Two residences in the Hammer Point subdivision of Tavernier experienced roof damage with tree, utility line and minor facade damage to other homes in the Blue Waters and Ocean Park neighborhoods."},"events":[{"begin":"2026-03-01T17:27Z","county":"Lincoln","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-01T17:27Z","endLat":35.913,"endLon":-97.0162,"episode":210600,"id":1314685,"injuries":0,"lat":35.913,"location":"4.33 NW Tryon","lon":-97.0162,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"A photo was shared. The location is approximate.","source":"Emergency Manager","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2026-03-01T17:33Z","county":"Lincoln","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-01T17:33Z","endLat":35.9172,"endLon":-96.9811,"episode":210600,"id":1314686,"injuries":0,"lat":35.9172,"location":"3.47 NNW Tryon","lon":-96.9811,"magnitude":1.25,"narrative":"The report was relayed through mPING.","source":"Public","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2026-03-01T17:52Z","county":"Cowley","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deat